{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rh1FbXzjwuYujbS8hkspKc","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# struct_self_consist_ie — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-14 11:47 UTC | 更新原因: Baseline 全部完成，4 GPU 实验已 ALLOCATED，exp-005 完成，更新近期任务\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\n系统比较 4 类置信信号（log-prob / exact-match / FK / SJ / voting_conf）在 IE test-time scaling 中的有效性。核心发现：structural consistency family (SJ + voting_conf) 在 NER 上 2.5x 优于 log-prob，但 RE 因复合错误传播所有信号退化。详见 paper_framing.md。\\\\n\\\\n## 当前阶段\\\\n**Research 阶段** — Baseline 全部完成（决定性正面），4 个 P0 GPU 实验已 ALLOCATED 等待执行。\\\\n\\\\n### Baseline 结论（exp-012/013/014，全部完成）\\\\n- **SJ >> log-prob**: NER ρ=0.383 vs 0.140 (Δ=+0.243), AUROC 0.689 vs 0.591\\\\n- **voting_conf ≈ SJ**: NER ρ=0.392 vs 0.383 (统计持平), RE ρ=0.340 vs 0.244 (voting 更优)\\\\n- **exact_match ≈ FK**: NER ρ=0.294 vs 0.259, 均弱于 SJ/voting\\\\n- **结论**: Structural consistency family (SJ + voting_conf) 远优于所有替代方案，framing 成立\\\\n\\\\n### exp-005 温度分析（完成）\\\\n- SJ 温度鲁棒性最强（NER Δρ=+0.005, RE Δρ=-0.010）\\\\n- FK 温度敏感（NER Δρ=+0.062, RE Δρ=-0.095）\\\\n- Conditional filtering >> temperature tuning（RE SJ: cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temp effect ±0.01）\\\\n- 推荐 T=1.0 + conditional filtering\\\\n\\\\n### MVP 结论\\\\n- NER: rho_sj=0.388, SJ>FK +12pp (p=2e-20) → PASS\\\\n- RE full: rho_sj=0.234 → FAIL | RE cond: rho_sj=0.372 → 强信号\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [x] Dream 1 分析 → 结构性问题识别\\\\n- [x] 修订 paper_framing.md + experiment_plan.yaml\\\\n- [x] Baseline 实验 (exp-012/013/014) — **决定性正面，SJ 贡献确认**\\\\n- [x] exp-005 温度敏感性分析 — 完成\\\\n- [x] logprob 脚本集成到 run_mvp_pilot.py（--collect_logprobs）\\\\n- [ ] **4 个 GPU 实验执行中**：exp-001 (SciERC N=16, cuda:0), exp-002 (CoNLL, cuda:1), exp-003 (WNUT, cuda:2), exp-007 (LLaMA, cuda:3)\\\\n- [ ] run_mvp_pilot.py `--dataset` 加 conll2003/wnut17 选项（exp-002/003 推理前置）\\\\n- [ ] exp-015 指标扩展（AUROC/τ/calibration 全信号全数据集）— CPU 进行中\\\\n- [ ] exp-004 RE 诊断分析（per-relation-type + bootstrap CI）— CPU 进行中\\\\n- [ ] Re-dream (dream_20260514T105303) — writing 阶段，不阻塞实验\\\\n- [ ] gpu-5090-4x-2 (4 GPU) 未使用 — exp-001 seed 123/456 + P1 实验候选\\\\n- [Dream 观察] inverted-U pattern 需用独立 proxy 验证，不过度宣称\\\\n- [Dream 观察] 跨数据集比较必须统一 N 和 T\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n8× RTX 5090 32GB（autodl-5090 4 GPU + gpu-5090-4x-2 4 GPU）\\\\n当前：autodl-5090 全部 4 GPU 已分配 P0 实验 | gpu-5090-4x-2 待分配（exp-001 多 seed / P1）\\\\n\\\\n## 时间线\\\\n- **目标**: EMNLP 2026 via ARR May, DDL **2026-05-25**（距今 11 天）\\\\n- ~~Baseline~~: 完成 | P0 GPU 实验: 今天~明天 | 论文写作: 2-3 天 | 迭代: 2-3 天\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D013 | 2026-05-14 | exp-013/014: voting confidence 与 SJ 持平(NER)/更优(RE) | exp_013_exact_match, exp_014_entity_voting |\\\\n| D012 | 2026-05-14 | exp-012 log-prob baseline: SJ 压倒性胜出 (NER Δρ=+0.217 | exp_012_logprob_baseline |\\\\n| D011 | 2026-05-14 | Dream 三档全 3/6 暴露结构性缺陷：缺强 baseline (log-prob/exact- | dream_20260514T093336 |\\\\n| D010 | 2026-05-14 | pilot_005 T=0.7 确认 RE full FAIL (rho=0.234<0.30)，但 | mvp_pilot_005, mvp_pilot_004, e1_component_wise_re_sj |\\\\n| D009 | 2026-05-14 | E1 否定乘性惩罚假说，方案 B 排除，确认走方案 A（NER-primary + RE 诊断） | e1_component_wise_re_sj, mvp_pilot_004 |\\\\n| D008 | 2026-05-14 | E1 否定乘性惩罚假设，Narrative B 排除，确认走 Narrative A (NER-pr | e1_component_wise_re_sj, mvp_pilot_004, mvp_pilot_005 |\\\\n| D007 | 2026-05-14 | Gate 1 FAIL (RE rho_sj=0.244<0.30), 但 T=1.0 zero r | mvp_pilot_004, mvp_pilot_003 |\\\\n| D006 | 2026-05-14 | Narrative 选择方案 A (stay-the-course)：等 ft_002_v2 改进  | mvp_pilot_001, ft_002 |\\\\n| D005 | 2026-05-14 | MVP pilot ft_001 结果：FAIL but positive signals. 等 f | ft_001 |\\\\n| D004 | 2026-05-14 | Gate 0: NER PASS (60.4%), RE FAIL (33.8%). 执行方案 C— | ft_001 |\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 3302, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SFrNhH828HyFPLsu8kbd3n","session_id":"e37c9bd6-dc13-41f5-9c3a-b482146d5201","uuid":"472dc615-7585-4e90-b6ca-d497f06424e3","timestamp":"2026-05-14T11:48:09.830Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F935oVxQsX9vJyEc3UsgKd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013J6oYcWdQtZjD2dEM9FJhZ","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"struct_self_consist_ie","file":"paper_framing.md","max_chars":0},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":17597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1105,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SFrNhH828HyFPLsu8kbd3n","session_id":"e37c9bd6-dc13-41f5-9c3a-b482146d5201","uuid":"1cb44453-4d1c-4944-83d1-5f056dab76f3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013J6oYcWdQtZjD2dEM9FJhZ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\\\\n\\\\n> Updated 2026-05-14 post-Dream analysis. Dream dream_20260514T093336 revealed structural issues (3/6 all tiers). Major revision: add strong baselines, reframe contribution, expand evaluation.\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR May 2026)\\\\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\\\\n- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (2 条)\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 1 (Positive — NER)\\\\nSampling-based structural consistency signals (soft Jaccard, entity voting confidence) provide dramatically stronger confidence signals for entity-level IE than both model confidence (sequence log-probability, AUROC≈0.59) and surface agreement (Fleiss' Kappa, exact-match voting). SJ and voting confidence are statistically comparable on NER (ρ≈0.39), but SJ generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs beyond entity sets.\\\\n\\\\n**Key insight**: The contribution is about a FAMILY of structural consistency signals, not one specific metric. SJ and voting_conf both capture entity-across-sample consistency at different granularity — their convergence on NER shows the underlying signal is robust. SJ's advantage is generalizability (works for any structured output); voting's advantage is simplicity (no pairwise comparison needed).\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence**: NER full: SJ ρ=0.383, voting_conf ρ=0.392, FK ρ=0.259, logprob ρ=0.140. NER cond: SJ ρ=0.412 (unique signal >0.40). Structural consistency family is 2.5x stronger than log-prob. RE full: voting_conf ρ=0.340 > SJ ρ=0.244 (voting more robust with sparse tuples).\\\\n\\\\n### Claim 2 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\\\\nThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks fundamentally degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested (SJ, FK, log-prob, exact-match).\\\\n\\\\n**MVP evidence**: RE full rho_sj=0.234, RE cond rho_sj=0.372 (SJ>FK +11.8pp). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n\\\\n**Problem**: Test-time scaling (TTS) through sampling + selection requires a reliable confidence signal. Self-consistency has shown promise in reasoning tasks (majority voting), but structured prediction (IE) poses unique challenges: outputs have internal structure (entities, relations, triplets), and it is unclear which confidence signals — model confidence (log-prob), surface agreement (exact-match/FK), or structural similarity (SJ) — best correlate with output quality.\\\\n\\\\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency in LLM reasoning uses exact-match voting (Wang et al. 2023). Universal Self-Consistency (Chen et al. NAACL 2024) extends this to non-votable outputs via LLM-as-judge. For structured prediction, no systematic comparison exists across confidence signal families (model-internal vs surface vs structural) for TTS selection. Semantic uncertainty methods (Kuhn et al. ICML 2023) cluster outputs by equivalence but don't leverage structural similarity.\\\\n\\\\n**Our framing**: We systematically compare four families of confidence signals for IE test-time scaling: (1) model confidence (sequence log-probability), (2) surface agreement (Fleiss' Kappa, exact-match voting rate), (3) set-aware structural similarity (soft Jaccard), and (4) entity-level majority voting. We discover that set-aware consistency outperforms all alternatives for entity-level tasks, but ALL signals degrade for relational tasks due to compound error propagation. This establishes both the best-practice confidence signal for NER TTS and a principled task-complexity boundary for consistency-based TTS in structured prediction.\\\\n\\\\n**Headline result template**: \\\\\\\"On three NER datasets, set-aware self-consistency (soft Jaccard) achieves rho=0.39-0.45 correlation with accuracy, outperforming sequence log-probability (rho=X), exact-match voting (rho=Y), and Fleiss' Kappa (rho=0.26-0.32), yielding +Zpp F1 via best-of-N selection. However, on relation extraction, all confidence signals degrade (full-set rho<0.28), with conditional analysis revealing a task-complexity boundary governed by compound error propagation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\\\\n\\\\n### R1: \\\\\\\"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-002 (CoNLL-2003) + exp-003 (WNUT-17) validate cross-dataset across 3 domains (science/news/social media)\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R2: \\\\\\\"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R3: \\\\\\\"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK ≈ exact-match. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\\\\n- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\\\\n\\\\n### R3b: \\\\\\\"Voting confidence matches or beats SJ — why use SJ?\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: SJ generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events, any set-structured prediction). Voting is entity-specific. NER: statistically equivalent. RE: voting more robust with sparse tuples. Paper presents both as valid instantiations of the structural consistency principle.\\\\n- **Priority**: Addressed by framing\\\\n\\\\n### R4: \\\\\\\"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-006 (adaptive compute demo) — SJ vs log-prob vs FK vs random best-of-N selection on all NER datasets\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R5: \\\\\\\"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R6: \\\\\\\"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\\\\n- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\\\\n\\\\n### R7: \\\\\\\"Only ρ as evaluation metric\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots, Kendall's τ for all experiments\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R8: \\\\\\\"Formula-implementation discrepancy\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\\\\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\\\\n\\\\n### R9: \\\\\\\"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\\\\n- **Priority**: P0\\\\n\\\\n### R10: \\\\\\\"Insufficient related work\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Mitigation**: Expand to 30+ references. Must cite: USC (Chen 2024), semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Desai & Durrett 2020), SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017).\\\\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit\\\\n\\\\nEMNLP is well-suited for:\\\\n- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\\\\n- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\\\\n- The \\\\\\\"comparison + boundary condition\\\\\\\" contribution pattern\\\\n\\\\nRisk: If SJ doesn't beat log-prob, the paper becomes a pure analysis piece. Mitigation: diagnostic framework (Claim 2) remains valid regardless; reframe as \\\\\\\"systematic study of confidence signals for IE TTS.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 7447, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SFrNhH828HyFPLsu8kbd3n","session_id":"e37c9bd6-dc13-41f5-9c3a-b482146d5201","uuid":"195b876b-cd22-4d5c-b2cf-90778b56b6c2","timestamp":"2026-05-14T11:48:10.230Z"}
